<section class="section" id="idea" aria-labelledby="idea-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
    <h2 id="idea-title">One spot, three senses</h2>
    <p>
      Most camera traps only take pictures. FALCON also listens and measures, because each sense covers
      what the others miss. It is meant for one well-chosen spot where animals come back again and again:
      a water bowl, a bird bath, the edge of a small pond. It is not a census and it is not a security camera.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="falcon-senses">
    <article class="falcon-sense">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 12s3.5-6.5 9.5-6.5 9.5 6.5 9.5 6.5-3.5 6.5-9.5 6.5S2.5 12 2.5 12Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg>
      <h3><span>Lens</span>It sees what comes to the water</h3>
      <p>
        A 1080p camera with infrared lights watches the bowl by day and by night. Software finds animals in
        the picture and suggests a name from the 1,382 species recorded in Rajasthan on iNaturalist.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="falcon-sense">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 10v4M8 6.5v11M12 3.5v17M16 7.5v9M20 10.5v3"/></svg>
      <h3><span>Acoustic</span>It hears what never comes into view</h3>
      <p>
        Microphones in the box listen all the time. Bird calls are named and grouped into calling bouts, so
        one bird singing for ten minutes is one record. At night it logs calls the camera cannot see.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="falcon-sense">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10 13.8V5a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v8.8a4 4 0 1 1-4 0Z"/><path d="M12 9v7"/></svg>
      <h3><span>Climate</span>It notes the weather of every visit</h3>
      <p>
        Temperature, humidity and air pressure are read every 30 seconds, and a plate on top says whether it
        is wet. Each record is stored with the weather at that moment.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

